# Before the first scene, and cut from the recording: the window comes forward, and
# every page a scene shows is loaded once, so no scene waits on the network.
# The coordinates are read from shots/setup-03-open.png of a layout run.
activate
wait 4
# Django, the first pinned row, at y = 156.
glide 700 600 150 156 0.6
click 150 156
wait 3
# PyPI, the second pinned row, at y = 201. Close the notice across its top, if it shows
# one (at (1367, 69); in October 2026 a security notice), so its blue header is the top
# edge the row takes; without a notice the click lands on the header's empty end.
click 150 201
wait 3
click 1367 69
wait 1.5
# The sample app on localhost, at y = 493.
click 150 493
wait 2.5
# The other Spaces' pages, found by title in the command bar: the map in Personal,
# then Reading's two, Apollo 11 last so it is Reading's page on screen when the spaces
# scene arrives there.
key t+cmd
wait 1
type OpenStreetMap
wait 1.5
key down
wait 0.5
key enter
wait 5
# Close the map's side panels, its October promotion (at (672, 553)) and then its
# welcome (at (685, 166)), so the map fills the page; on a day without them the
# clicks land on the map and the panel's ground, which take no action.
click 672 553
wait 1
click 685 166
wait 1.5
key t+cmd
wait 1
type NASA
wait 1.5
key down
wait 0.5
key enter
wait 4
key t+cmd
wait 1
type Apollo 11
wait 1.5
key down
wait 0.5
key enter
wait 3
# Back to Work by its chip (the first of three, at the sidebar's foot), then its
# GitHub essential, the first essentials card at (51, 71).
click 150 848
wait 2.5
click 51 71
wait 3
# The rest point, on the sidebar's empty ground (150, 720). Every glide after
# this one starts where the step before left the pointer.
glide 150 720 0.6
wait 2
